{"type": "concept", "subtype": "symptom", "title": "AD 症状：似乎没有在听", "content": "AD 症状之一：经常在别人跟他说话时没有在听，不是因为专心看电视或拼乐高，也不是因为不想听，而是好像没有能力专心听人说话。", "steps": [], "conditions": [], "limits": [], "modules": ["专注力"], "tags": ["ADHD", "症状", "倾听"], "evidence": "course_claim", "risk_flags": [], "id": "s-0713043f1cc2-c001:a007", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "s-0713043f1cc2", "blocks": ["b00009"], "source_kind": "A1"}, {"source_id": "s-0713043f1cc2", "blocks": ["b00009"], "source_kind": "A1"}], "review_status": "point_source_reviewed", "version": "2026-11-05.full-2", "relations": [{"target": "s-0713043f1cc2-c001:a017", "kind": "association", "condition": "无", "reason": "“AD 症状：似乎没有在听”是AD症状之一，“AD 诊断的症状数量标准”规定16岁以内至少六点症状、16岁以上至少五点症状。单个症状只是计数标准中的一个要素，不是该标准的直接例子，故改为关联。", "evidence": "knowledge_synthesis", "review_status": "revised", "review_notes": "原 example_of 不成立，单个症状不足以作为诊断数量标准的例子。"}], "knowledge_units": ["s-0713043f1cc2-c001:u0011"], "retrieval_scope": "knowledge", "knowledge_layer": "expanded", "alternate_titles": []}
